          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "The quiet layoffs sweeping China's tech giants as Alibaba cuts headcount by a third amid AI pivot",
            "articleSection": "Job Evolution",
            "abstract": "China's largest tech companies are conducting sweeping but low-profile workforce reductions as they pivot aggressively toward AI-first business models. Alibaba reduced its headcount by approximately one third in 2025, while Baidu's workforce declined by nearly 7 percent. Workers inside these companies describe an environment of constant churn, with roles being eliminated faster than AI-adjacent positions are being created.",
            "url": "https://restofworld.org/2026/china-tech-layoffs-alibaba-baidu-ai-pivot/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=feeds",
